          "title": "DHCP and the DORA Exchange",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What DHCP Hands Out",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Auto-assigns ==IP address==, ==subnet mask==, ==default gateway==, ==DNS server==",
                "Runs over ==UDP==: server port {blue:67}, client port {green:68}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. DORA and a Trace",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Discover",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Offer",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Request",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ack",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Step",
                "From",
                "Detail"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Discover",
                  "client",
                  "broadcast, `0.0.0.0` → `255.255.255.255`"
                ],
                [
                  "Offer",
                  "server",
                  "proposes an IP"
                ],
                [
                  "Request",
                  "client",
                  "broadcast, accepts one offer"
                ],
                [
                  "Acknowledge",
                  "server",
                  "confirms, ==lease starts=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Request is ==broadcast on purpose==",
                "Other servers that offered see it, learn they lost, and **free** their address"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Trace",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client 0.0.0.0 sends Discover",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server 192.168.1.1 offers 192.168.1.50/24",
                    "note": "gw 192.168.1.1, lease 24h",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Client Requests it",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server ACKs",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotcha",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Two DHCP servers on one LAN",
              "text": "A rogue home router hands out ==conflicting gateways/DNS==, so connectivity fails **randomly**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Leases, Renewal and Relays",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Leases, Renewal and Relays",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Lease Timers",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Lease starts",
                    "sub": "Ack received",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T1 = 50%",
                    "sub": "unicast Request, same server",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T2 = 87.5%",
                    "sub": "broadcast Request, any server",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Expiry",
                    "sub": "drop IP, restart DORA",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==DHCPRELEASE==: client hands the address back early",
                "==DHCPDECLINE==: client's ARP check found the offered IP already in use"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Relay Agent",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Routers do not forward broadcasts",
                "Relay turns the broadcast into **unicast** to the server",
                "It stamps ==giaddr== so the server picks the right scope"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "text",
              "lines": [
                "interface Vlan20",
                " ip helper-address 10.0.0.5"
              ],
              "note": "on the router interface facing the clients"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which Setup?",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Relay?",
                "Rule"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Server on same subnet",
                  "No",
                  "broadcast reaches it"
                ],
                [
                  "Remote subnet",
                  "Yes",
                  "one scope per subnet"
                ],
                [
                  "Reservation",
                  "As for its subnet",
                  "MAC bound to a fixed IP"
                ],
                [
                  "Static IP",
                  "No",
                  "set on host, outside pool"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Static inside the pool",
              "text": "The server may lease that address again, giving a ==duplicate IP==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ICMP Message Types and Ping",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ICMP Message Types and Ping",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What ICMP Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Layer 3== control protocol, IP protocol number ==1==",
                "Reports **errors** and diagnostics",
                "No ports"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Key Message Types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Name"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "0",
                  "Echo Reply"
                ],
                [
                  "3",
                  "Destination Unreachable"
                ],
                [
                  "5",
                  "Redirect"
                ],
                [
                  "8",
                  "Echo Request"
                ],
                [
                  "11",
                  "Time Exceeded"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Type 3 codes: `0` net, `1` host, `3` port",
                "`4` = ==fragmentation needed and DF set=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Ping",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Echo Request",
                    "sub": "type 8",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Echo Reply",
                    "sub": "type 0",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Output shows ==TTL==, ==round-trip time== and ==packet loss %=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Linux/macOS",
                "Windows"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Send 4",
                  "`ping -c 4 host`",
                  "`ping -n 4 host`"
                ],
                [
                  "Payload size",
                  "`-s`",
                  "`-l`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No reply is not down",
              "text": "Firewalls often drop ICMP echo. **Ping fails but TCP works** is common."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
